  "content": {
    "id": "v2-8-practice-section-slot-7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Two bodies move along a straight path, starting at the same time, so their displacement $x$ m from a fixed point $O$ at any time $t$ is given by $x=t^2-6t+10$ and $x=2t-5$ respectively. At what times are they:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-8-practice-section-slot-7-slot-7-q-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Together.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=3\\text{ s}$ and $t=5\\text{ s}$.",
          "worked": "The bodies are together when their displacements are equal.\n$$\\begin{align*}t^2-6t+10&=2t-5\\\\t^2-8t+15&=0\\\\(t-3)(t-5)&=0\\\\t&=3\\text{ or }5\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values satisfy $t\\geq0$. Hence $t=3\\text{ s}$ and $t=5\\text{ s}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-8-practice-section-slot-7-slot-7-q-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Travelling with the same velocity?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=4\\text{ s}$.",
          "worked": "Differentiating the displacement functions gives $v_1=2t-6$ and $v_2=2$. For equal velocities,\n$$\\begin{align*}2t-6&=2\\\\2t&=8\\\\t&=4\\text{ s}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
